00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:35.380
episode

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:35.380
"On the Morning of
\hthe Duel, Will Oscar...?"

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:48.910
What's all this?

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:50.380
You weren't aware?

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:51.140
No.

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:55.510
They're the people from Rose Bertin's
dressmaking shop in Paris.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.250
They began coming to the palace recently.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.220
Lady Antoinette is really fond of their work.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.990
Do those boxes all have dresses inside?

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:05.830
Most likely.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.830
The Minister of Finance was heard lamenting...

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:13.270
...about how the payments to Bertin's shop
have been exorbitant these past two months.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:18.770
Don't you think Lady Antoinette's spending
habits are a bit excessive, Oscar?

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:29.140
Well then, Your Majesty, please
have a look at these designs.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:33.790
My!

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:39.430
If Your Majesty wore this to an evening soirée,
there'd be at least 50 men who would faint!

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:42.990
This one is called ''The Secret Sigh.''

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:45.530
My! Such a magnificent color!

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.000
It suits you so well.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:52.170
But I already had 18 formal dresses and
38 evening gowns made last month.

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:54.540
Nonsense!

00:03:54.540 --> 00:04:00.090
The Queen must always be at the
forefront of the latest trends, and...

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:04.180
You must serve as a role model
for the rest of high society.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.320
Of course.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:06.790
She's right.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:07.920
True...

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:09.060
Instead of this color,

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.630
I think it'd look better if it were
made with that brown silk.

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:12.640
What do you think?

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.060
Certainly, Your Majesty!

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.970
Such impeccable taste.

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:18.970
I'm sure that would look wonderful.

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:20.440
How envious.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:21.530
Your Majesty.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:23.570
Oh, it's been a while, Oscar!

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:28.310
I've been waiting for you every day.

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:32.590
You haven't shown your face lately, so is there something you're upset with?

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:34.770
No, Your Majesty.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:38.350
Say, André, what do you think of this color?

00:04:38.350 --> 00:04:39.510
Isn't it a lovely brown?

00:04:40.090 --> 00:04:43.510
T-To me it looks like the color
of a flea, Your Majesty.

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:45.730
The color of a flea?!

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:46.360
How dare you!

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.070
Color of a flea? Flea color...?

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:51.130
Très Bien!

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:52.480
I like that!

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:57.170
Then, why don't you also differentiate the colors
of the flea's stomach and legs for that matter?

00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:59.150
That's it, Your Majesty!

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:01.410
What a brilliant idea!

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:05.470
This year's trend color will be flea color!

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:09.790
I'd also like some flea colored
fabrics, Madame Bertin.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:14.620
Please make me a flea's stomach colored dress.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.090
I'd like some flea colored undergarments!

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:17.090
I'd like a flea colored corset!

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:19.530
Flea color!

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.270
This is ridiculous!

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:24.560
Who cares about their flea color!

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:26.930
It's starting to get itchy, isn't it?

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.870
Now that she's Queen, there are plenty of mindful topics...

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:32.890
...she could concern herself with,
such as our nation and its people.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:37.190
Yet, day after day, all she does
is pursue her own enjoyment.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:39.920
You once said it yourself.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:41.650
All the money Lady Antoinette spends,

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.250
comes directly from the people's taxes.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:47.860
Yet, she spends it on plays, balls, dresses...!

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:49.690
Wasting it all away!

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:51.830
André, at least for now, don't be so harsh.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:53.660
How come?

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:58.930
You were the one who was worried how
the people might regard Lady Antoinette.

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:02.660
I did say that, but for now...

00:06:03.970 --> 00:06:08.720
I want to let Lady Antoinette do as she
pleases just for a little while longer.

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:13.010
She is lonely.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:18.150
What would a rose smile at, if it lost its sun?

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.310
Without the stars or the moon,

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:23.040
what would a sailor sail his ship
towards, out in the open seas?

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.960
Are you referring to Hans Axel von Fersen?

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:28.600
By adorning herself and being absorbed in plays,

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:31.000
she is trying to bury her loneliness.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:32.630
I want you to understand that.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:35.240
All right, let's hurry.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.830
I need to check on the preparations
for tomorrow's luncheon.

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:46.050
Schönbrunn Palace

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:50.010
What...

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.920
What has become of her?!

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:55.100
She has become even more beautiful
and dignified, hasn't she?

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:57.270
How could this be considered beautiful?!

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:00.980
This isn't a portrait of the Queen of France!

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:03.440
It's a painting of a flashy actress!

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:05.700
I see, but...

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:10.400
To think this foolish and gaudily
dressed woman is my daughter...

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:15.110
Send this awful painting back
to France immediately.

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:24.810
<i>My dear Marie...</i>

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:28.820
<i>She is taken by jewelry and
feathered accessories...</i>

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:32.830
<i>Does she even know the enormous
amount of tax money...</i>

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:35.130
<i>...that is being spent to acquire those things?</i>

00:07:36.630 --> 00:07:37.930
<i>Mother Mary...</i>

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:39.850
<i>Please...</i>

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.630
<i>Please protect her.</i>

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:49.340
You seem so happy, Marie Antoinette.

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:51.780
You are becoming even more beautiful.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.550
The Fairy of Versailles.

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:54.780
The Queen of Rococo.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.450
The French Rose.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.910
All those whispers intoxicate me with joy.

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:06.190
And yet, what is this feeling in my heart,
as if I were missing something?

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:09.760
Tell me, Mother.

00:08:10.670 --> 00:08:14.050
What is this feeling in my heart?

00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:40.760
Oh, a 1692 Château d'Yquem.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:42.000
Very nice.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.570
'91 was a bad year.

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:46.470
Probably because it rained too much.

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:50.440
Furthermore, the proprietor of the Bordeaux
region during the 80s was powerless.

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:52.670
He was too lenient on the peasants.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:55.930
That affects the flavor of the wine?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:57.380
Indeed, it does.

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:59.180
The peasantry must be worked to the bone,

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:01.720
kept neither dead nor alive,
in order to make a fine product.

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:06.380
We wouldn't be able to fill our stomachs
with delicious food, if they were lazy!

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:13.030
By the way, I am thinking about
canceling the morning audience...

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:15.530
...and the general audience with the public.

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:16.460
May I hear your thoughts?

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:19.830
A fine idea. We can sleep in.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:23.290
If we don't have an audience on Tuesdays,
we can go hunting from the morning.

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:26.240
Duke de Guéméné, what are
your thoughts on this matter?

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:28.200
Fine with me.

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.510
Actually, it's a swell idea.

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:33.130
There is no need...

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:38.350
...for the Queen of France, of all people,
to give an audience to such lowly people.

00:09:38.350 --> 00:09:41.420
I suggest you stop immediately.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.100
However...!

00:09:42.390 --> 00:09:44.060
What is it, Oscar?

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:48.600
It seems the members of the Royal Guards
aren't instructed on manners these days.

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:52.320
How dare a mere guard interrupt
a discussion amongst royals!

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.900
It's all right.

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:56.500
Oscar is my friend.

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:58.240
Speak your mind, Oscar.

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:02.290
With all due respect, putting the topic of your audience with the nobles aside,

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:06.750
the general audiences with the public
is your duty as King and Queen.

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:07.920
Duty?

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:13.380
The people have traveled great distances to
visit the palace and by addressing them,

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:16.850
their understanding and affections
for you will grow deeper.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:21.100
Furthermore, it's an opportunity for Your Majesty...

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:24.330
...to learn about matters outside the palace,
such as the countryside and your people.

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:25.400
So, please...

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:26.430
I understand.

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:31.400
I implore you to not sever your
bond with your subjects.

00:10:32.010 --> 00:10:34.360
I will follow your advice, Oscar.

00:10:34.810 --> 00:10:37.210
Thank you, Your Majesty.

00:10:42.470 --> 00:10:45.650
My, how beautiful.

00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:49.370
This pistol is the latest Corel-style model.

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:51.840
It's lightweight and has precision aim.

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:55.190
I hear you're quite the sharpshooter,
Duke de Guéméné.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:57.170
Not at all.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:11:02.470
However, if you'd like to see,
I can shoot an ace card 50 toise away.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:03.800
My, how amazing.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:05.810
I'm confident in my sharp shooting skills,

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:10.270
compared to those of some greenhorn,
who blabbers on without knowing their place!

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:13.900
She may be the daughter of a general,

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:17.320
but a mere woman as the
Regiment Commander of the Royal Guards?!

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:18.680
It's completely absurd!

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:21.450
This, coming from you?

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:25.330
A child, who doesn't know the
difference from right or wrong,

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:29.580
was lied to and shot from behind with a pistol,
and his shooter calls himself a Duke!

00:11:29.960 --> 00:11:31.370
That's what's absurd!

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:34.770
That child stole my money!

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:36.590
What's wrong with punishing a thief?!

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:41.310
The poor are always looking for
an opportunity to steal from us!

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:43.220
He deserved to be executed
and be made an example of!

00:11:44.110 --> 00:11:46.880
Even if a young child stole out of hunger,

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:49.480
none of us has the right to judge and punish him!

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:52.600
Or are you saying you are a God, Duke?!

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:54.190
H-How dare you!

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:55.920
Do you know who I am?!

00:11:57.060 --> 00:11:59.990
I'm Duke Henri Salvator de Guéméné!

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.160
You arrogant twerp!

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.130
You're the one who is arrogant!

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:07.070
Do you think you can get away with anything,
as long as you are a duke?!

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:08.450
You call yourself a noble?!

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:18.140
I, Oscar François, accept your challenge.

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:21.250
An observer will contact you
with the time and place.

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:22.070
Your weapon of choice?

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:24.130
I choose pistol, your specialty.

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:30.930
You better not back down at the last minute, twerp.

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:34.900
To this day, I, Oscar,
have never broken a promise!

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:35.830
Such insolence!

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:38.060
I'll put a bullet through
that beautiful face of yours!

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:55.500
Brilliantly done, Oscar.

00:12:59.740 --> 00:13:02.840
Why aren't you stopping her, Master?

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:03.840
Do not worry.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.580
As with sword, I have trained
her equally as well with a gun.

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:10.480
I wouldn't have raised her as my successor,
if she should die over something like this.

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:14.320
Tradition has it that the one who is
challenged can choose the weapon.

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:16.940
So why did Commander choose a pistol?

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:22.960
That's just how Oscar is.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:24.760
She never takes the easy way out.

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:26.570
A sword would have been an easy win for her.

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:31.600
I hear Duke de Guéméné came in second at
the shooting competition in Rome last year.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:46.250
See that?

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:47.690
There's nothing to be worried about.

00:13:47.690 --> 00:13:50.020
However, a duel is a one shot deal.

00:13:50.020 --> 00:13:51.320
If she were to miss...!

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:53.930
Also, Duke de Guéméné is a coward.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:55.930
Who knows what kind of trickery he might use.

00:13:55.930 --> 00:14:00.200
Well, that's precisely the reason
why observers will be present.

00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:01.830
Don't worry, don't worry.

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:18.850
A pistol duel against that greenhorn
is like taking candy from a baby.

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:21.220
Wouldn't you agree, Duke Orléans?

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:25.130
Something on your mind?

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:28.090
However, only one bullet may be used in a duel.

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:29.630
One bullet...

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:38.470
If, by chance you were to miss,
consider yourself dead.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.410
Although, there is a way to seal your victory,

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:51.040
but I doubt you would need such a thing.

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:53.330
Just what might that be?

00:14:54.090 --> 00:14:58.220
If I tell you, can I expect
something equal in return?

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.360
O-Of course.

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:02.920
So what were you suggesting?

00:15:07.300 --> 00:15:10.510
To say the duel were to take
place behind Chapel de Farge.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:11.640
A-And?

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:15.970
I know that area well, as I
walk there every morning.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:22.180
The forest path that leads to the back
of Chapel de Farge runs west to east.

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:27.140
During this time of year,
the sun rises from this path.

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:29.610
Interestingly,

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:34.580
one of the stained glass windows of this chapel, has been broken and tilted for as long as l can remember.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:36.540
When the sun rises,

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:38.560
it reflects off that tilted stained glass window,

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:40.960
and reflects down onto a
certain spot on the ground.

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:47.410
What would happen if that light
should shine on Oscar's face,

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:49.760
when she's about to fire her pistol?

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:00.980
If I, as the observer, decide your positions...

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:03.610
...and when the duel should start...

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:07.650
Oscar will have no chance of winning.

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:10.160
I see, I see...!

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:11.630
I appreciate this greatly.

00:16:23.510 --> 00:16:24.370
You can't sleep?

00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:27.040
It's not that.

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:28.310
Don't worry about it.

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:30.480
You'll win.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:31.780
I'm not worried.

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:33.380
I see.

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:34.760
Then, why don't you get some sleep already?

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:40.090
Do you remember, Oscar?

00:16:40.090 --> 00:16:41.490
When you were 7 years old,

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:45.360
we buried our treasures under that oak tree.

00:16:46.330 --> 00:16:47.870
I don't remember.

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:50.940
It was a large lead top and a red knife.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.240
I wonder if it's still there?

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:53.160
Who knows...

00:16:54.340 --> 00:16:56.570
Let's leave from the back gate tomorrow morning.

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:58.380
We'll never hear the end of it,
if Grandma finds out.

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:00.380
Girodelle is my observer.

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:01.640
You don't have to come.

00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:04.330
I'll accompany you.
At least, midway.

00:17:07.550 --> 00:17:08.720
Let's get some sleep.

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:10.410
You shouldn't let your shoulders get cold.

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:13.190
I guess you want to be alone.

00:17:13.190 --> 00:17:15.390
In that case, I'm going to bed.

00:17:15.390 --> 00:17:15.930
André...

00:17:17.900 --> 00:17:18.760
What is it?

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:19.390
Are you afraid?

00:17:19.960 --> 00:17:21.060
I'm not afraid.

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:25.030
No, I am afraid...

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:28.910
But it's not that I'm afraid of my opponent.

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:32.700
I'm afraid that I must take part
in an exchange of precious lives.

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:37.110
De Guéméné is a heinous man.

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:40.500
The weak and the farming peasantry are
nothing but insignificant worms to him.

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:45.560
Letting a man like him run loose will not only
disgrace every member of the nobility,

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:48.170
but will ultimately disgrace the image
of the royal family, as well.

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:52.130
But a life is a life...

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:56.090
No matter how heinous he might be,
I fear having to take someone's life.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:01.460
André, if I die...

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:05.440
The treasures buried beneath
the oak tree are yours.

00:18:06.060 --> 00:18:09.560
There's a lead top, a red knife and a stuffed bear...

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:15.740
Well, let's go to bed.
Good night.

00:19:04.640 --> 00:19:06.400
<i>Pierre!!</i>

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:24.010
Well then, the duel shall be conducted in accordance with the code of knighthood from ancient times.

00:19:28.160 --> 00:19:29.810
The duelists will stand back to back.

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:34.460
On my count, take ten steps, turn and fire.

00:19:35.430 --> 00:19:37.120
Why didn't you tell me this sooner?!

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:40.810
I heard it late last night, as well.

00:19:40.810 --> 00:19:41.840
I have to stop them!

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:43.700
How could Oscar be in a duel...?!

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:47.710
We will now begin the duel between
Duke Henri Salvator de Guéméné,

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:51.920
and Oscar François de Jarjayes,
Regiment Commander of the Royal Guards.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:56.090
The duel will be observed by
Duke Louis Philippe Joseph d'Orléans,

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:59.420
and Captain Victor Clément de Girodelle.

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:00.690
Begin!

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:02.450
Un!

00:20:05.460 --> 00:20:06.390
Go faster!

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:08.990
Trois!

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:13.830
Cinq!

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:17.190
God, please let me get there in time!

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:21.240
Sept!

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:25.750
Huit!

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:33.120
Neuf!

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:47.010
<i>The light is coming from behind?</i>

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:48.200
<i>How could that be?</i>

00:20:50.210 --> 00:20:52.210
<i>It's reflecting off the glass window of the chapel...!</i>

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:54.080
<i>If it's reflecting down over there,</i>

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:58.580
<i>that means the light will hit me directly in
the face and blind me when I turn around.</i>

00:20:58.580 --> 00:20:59.530
<i>I'm in trouble!</i>

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:02.490
I'll put a bullet through that
beautiful forehead of yours!

00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:04.150
Dix!

00:21:14.770 --> 00:21:16.550
<i>Aim for his wicked hand that shot that child!</i>

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:22.970
Are you all right, Oscar?!

00:21:26.710 --> 00:21:28.680
My hand...! My hand...!

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:28.680
It's all right.

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:29.970
It's not a life-threatening injury.

00:21:34.220 --> 00:21:35.390
Oscar!

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:37.520
You used some underhanded tactic, didn't you?!

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:39.200
There must be a trick of some sort!

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:41.430
Don't underestimate me!

00:21:41.430 --> 00:21:42.860
I am a duke!

00:21:44.730 --> 00:21:45.700
Oscar!

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:47.700
Do you know what you have done?!

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:50.040
You are to be on disciplinary confinement
for the next month!

00:21:52.170 --> 00:21:53.640
Duke de Guéméné.

00:21:53.640 --> 00:21:57.570
Don't you think it's shameful for a noble
like yourself, to lose such self-control?

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:05.280
That's terrible.

00:22:05.280 --> 00:22:06.410
It's completely unfair.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:08.810
The punishment is too severe!

00:22:12.420 --> 00:22:14.520
<i>Oscar, forgive me.</i>

00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:16.790
<i>Unless I do this,</i>

00:22:16.790 --> 00:22:20.700
<i>I won't be able to keep those
who wish to entrap you at bay.</i>

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:31.790
To be continued

